const sourceReadings=[["Reframing unhelpful thoughts", "NHS", "The NHS explains how to notice an unhelpful thought, check the evidence and consider another interpretation. Read it with one ordinary situation in mind.", "Takeaway: write what happened separately from what you think it means.", "https://www.nhs.uk/every-mind-matters/mental-wellbeing-tips/self-help-cbt-techniques/reframing-unhelpful-thoughts/"], ["Tackling your worries", "NHS", "This guide separates actionable problems from hypothetical worries and explains a short planned period for considering them. You can try one approach and see whether it fits your day.", "Takeaway: choose a practical next step, or note what you cannot resolve now.", "https://www.nhs.uk/every-mind-matters/mental-wellbeing-tips/self-help-cbt-techniques/tackling-your-worries/"], ["What is retrieval practice?", "Dr. Pooja Agarwal / Retrieval Practice", "An educator guide to learning by bringing information to mind before checking it. It offers a useful companion to your Portuguese recall exercise.", "Takeaway: attempt one phrase from memory, then use the answer to correct it.", "https://www.retrievalpractice.org/retrievalpractice"], ["Implementation intentions", "National Cancer Institute", "A research overview of plans that connect a recognizable situation with an intended action. This is a deeper read with research references.", "Takeaway: specify when you will start, not only what you hope to do.", "https://cancercontrol.cancer.gov/brp/research/constructs/implementation-intentions"]];
